      "end_reason": "eos_token",
      "raw_text": "To determine how many hours Tyler needs to work, we will follow these steps:\n\n**Step 1: Calculate the total cost of the books.**\nTyler wants to buy three items:\n1.  Dictionary: $18\n2.  Dinosaur book: $13\n3.  Children's cookbook: $8\n\nTotal Cost = $18 + $13 + $8\nTotal Cost = $31 + $8\nTotal Cost = $39\n\n**Step 2: Calculate the additional money Tyler needs.**\nTyler has already saved $14. We subtract this from the total cost to find out how much more he needs to earn.\n\nMoney Needed = Total Cost - Money Saved\nMoney Needed = $39 - $14\nMoney Needed = $25\n\n**Step 3: Calculate the number of hours Tyler needs to work.**\nTyler earns $5 per hour. We divide the money he still needs by his hourly wage.\n\nHours Needed = Money Needed / Hourly Wage\nHours Needed = $25 / $5\nHours Needed = 5\n\nTyler needs to work 5 hours to afford his books.\n\n#### 5<|im_end|>",
      "answer_text": "To determine how many hours Tyler needs to work, we will follow these steps:\n\n**Step 1: Calculate the total cost of the books.**\nTyler wants to buy three items:\n1.  Dictionary: $18\n2.  Dinosaur book: $13\n3.  Children's cookbook: $8\n\nTotal Cost = $18 + $13 + $8\nTotal Cost = $31 + $8\nTotal Cost = $39\n\n**Step 2: Calculate the additional money Tyler needs.**\nTyler has already saved $14. We subtract this from the total cost to find out how much more he needs to earn.\n\nMoney Needed = Total Cost - Money Saved\nMoney Needed = $39 - $14\nMoney Needed = $25\n\n**Step 3: Calculate the number of hours Tyler needs to work.**\nTyler earns $5 per hour. We divide the money he still needs by his hourly wage.\n\nHours Needed = Money Needed / Hourly Wage\nHours Needed = $25 / $5\nHours Needed = 5\n\nTyler needs to work 5 hours to afford his books.\n\n#### 5",
